"""
## Purpose and audience

This specification is maintained for compiler and library engineers reviewing SYSTEM-APP behavior, and for operators verifying a build.

## Operator workflow

Run `bin/simple test --no-session-daemon test/system/app/tooling/feature/warning_allow_root_cause_cleanup_spec.spl` and confirm the Results line reports 0 failed. Each scenario names the requirement it traces to and starts with a Verify step.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers only the behavior explicitly asserted below on the current toolchain. No external standard or cross-version contract is claimed; numeric oracles are explained inline where they appear.

## Recovery and troubleshooting

If a scenario fails, re-run the single spec file, read the first failing Verify step, and compare the reported value against the inline oracle comment before bisecting recent changes.
"""
# @manual: primary
# REQ-SYSTEM-APP-001
# doc-path: doc/01_research/app/
# doc-path: doc/03_plan/app/
# doc-path: doc/04_architecture/app/
# doc-path: doc/05_design/app/
# Warning/Allow Root-Cause Cleanup Spec

## Scenario: Rust strict lane targets the real workspace
- Given the repository workflow configuration
- When the Rust warning gate runs
- Then it uses `src/compiler_rust` as its workspace root

## Scenario: Simple strict lane is authoritative
- Given the repository workflow configuration
- When the Simple strict lint lane runs
- Then it executes `--deny-all` over the warning/allow cleanup canaries

## Scenario: Primitive-sort strict Rust baseline compiles
- Given the runtime primitive-sort module
- When strict Rust linting builds test targets
- Then the module exposes the NEON threshold constants referenced by its tests
